@brief Sets the base folder used to resolve project-relative '//<folder>/<file>' paths on EXPORT/SAVE
APIs. A path like '//USD/out.usd' then resolves to '<basePath>/USD/out.usd' (the whole remainder
is appended, so multi-level paths like '//A/B/C/out.usd' work too). Opening a project sets this
automatically to the project's folder; call this to override it (e.g. in a headless script or to
redirect output). Full/absolute paths are unaffected. Note: while a base is set, EVERY '//' path
is treated as project-relative (never as a UNC server or home folder); pass a full/mounted path
for those. '//' resolution applies to export/save paths only - IMPORT paths (e.g. ImportFile)
are NOT resolved; pass a full path when importing. Pass an empty string to clear it.
@param _basePath: the base folder, e.g. "C:/CLO/Test/Project".
